zigmkay_companion extraction provenance

The S08 desktop practice, lesson text, editor model, assignments and build
debounce are extracted from the unchanged reference paths under
zigmkay-companion/src/editor/. They retain the repository's GPLv2 provenance.
Historical source fixtures preserve original whitespace deliberately as
byte-exact project data.
The input-source package also retains the reference zkeymap LICENSE and exact
macOS/Windows/Linux C bridge bytes. Window, font and folder-dialog Zig adapters
are carried with the same GPLv2 provenance. The lazy pinned FreeType dependency
retains its upstream license files; release bundles must include its attribution.

The zqlite dependency is pinned to karlseguin/zqlite.zig revision
865223b734a5113f731ab1eb1d7d81c8ac252913 and retains its MIT license.
It supplies the Zig database API and bundled public-domain SQLite implementation.
The legacy keymap API shares the input-source package's implementation and native
bridges; duplicate bridge copies were removed without changing the retained bytes.

The migration reference is conlorz/zigmkay_firmware at
4755dac978658d10fd9b3bd13a184a1e1198b975 (local/monorepo).
Its implementation baseline is 3ee4135d308f18f15cc51b1d73e33e1b36bf517f;
the intervening changes are planning documents only.

LICENSE is copied verbatim from that repository (GNU GPL version 2).
No host implementation has been imported at bootstrap. Preserve existing
copyright/license notices when importing source. Dependency notices and asset
licenses must accompany their eventual imports; this file is not a complete
release attribution inventory.

The selected firmware dependency is the published EuroZig/zigmkay_firmware
PR #1 head at e122f7502df4ad58e831f0b37439085774b670cb, pinned with an
immutable package hash in build.zig.zon. It supports all 14 firmware selectors
as source; this is not a native release or an accepted stable contract.

